    "turn_text": "moment. And maybe that would have happened if I'd been on the debate stage. Maybe America would have looked up there and said, well, not sure, but what about that guy? That's what everyone was thinking on those debate stages. But in Oregon, I couldn't be on the ballot for both. And I didn't want to do what Marco Rubio did, campaign for the presidency, and then pivot to a different race, at least not as a plan. And so, and I also felt no matter who is in the Oval Office, if we do not fix the Senate, then our country is in total trouble. Because whether Mitch McConnell is the majority leader or the minority leader, He will completely continue his strategy obstruction. When he started it, I thought it wouldn't work and the American people would reject it and they didn't and he gained power and he's used that power. He has done deep damage to the court. He stole a Supreme Court seat. It's his proudest moment in his life. I did a 15 and a half hour speech to protest Technically, it wasn't a filibuster because at the moment he put the nomination on the floor, the Supreme Court nomination, at that very moment he filed for culture, which meant it already pre-scheduled the vote. So there was no actual way to delay the vote. I just wanted to stand up there and say, that look, this is an enormous mistake for America. Once you do this, you undermine the integrity of the court. So come together, there were several compromise ideas laid out. Come together, majority leader, minority leader. Figure it out because if this day passes and this Neil Gorsuch is confirmed, the credibility of the court as a fair body is deeply damaged and there's no right answer in the future. What's the right answer in the future? Is there a right answer in the future? for the Democrats to steal a seat back? Well, then you just have warfare. But if they don't steal a seat back, they don't balance out the first crime. I mean, there's no right answer. So I said, don't do this. And I can repeat that a lot in 15 hours and 30 minutes. I team had compiled all these articles and you know I started at 6 p.m. in the evening so I'd already been up all day so it was I must say not an exercise I plan to repeat I have so many inappropriate questions about how one does that but um You mentioned that you did not drink for 24 hours. You mentioned that you didn't want to be one of two dozen people up there without too much hope to actually be the nominee. Kirsten Gillibrand dropped out today. Who else should drop out now? Well, I'm not encouraging anyone to drop out. I mean, what",
